<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net48</TargetFramework>
    <AssemblyName>CasualtiesUnknownOnline.BulkTransfer.Core</AssemblyName>
    <Product>Bulk Transfer Core</Product>
    <Version>0.1.0</Version>
    <LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>CasualtiesUnknownOnline.BulkTransfer.Core</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The bulk-transfer capability the music ticket asked to be built as its OWN thing, not inside the player: a
    sender that slices a file into bounded chunks, a receiver that reassembles them, resume by the indices still
    missing, and one integrity verdict on the whole file. Deliberately no reference at all - plain C# over
    byte arrays - so the rules are testable without a session, and the mod that ships the player is the first
    consumer rather than the owner.
  -->
</Project>
